$ whycant -u alice exec /tmp/build.sh

✗ alice (uid 1000) cannot exec /tmp/build.sh

  /               drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /tmp            drwxrwxrwt  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /tmp/build.sh   -rwxr-xr-x  alice:alice  ✗ exec   ← blocked here

Why
  /tmp/build.sh is on /tmp, which is mounted noexec: files there cannot be run
  directly, not even by root. Passing a script to its interpreter still works
  (for example: sh /tmp/build.sh).

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Remount it with exec (noexec is often set on purpose, e.g. for /tmp):
       sudo mount -o remount,exec /tmp
